Background (from the session that started this one):
Interview task (Ender Turing): add Admin/Manager/Member role-based access to the Full-Stack FastAPI Template (FastAPI, SQLModel, Alembic, Postgres, React/TanStack, Playwright). Treated as a deployed app with existing users created via `is_superuser`. Plan under discussion:
- a `role` column backfilled from `is_superuser` (admin if superuser, else member);
- permissions mapped from roles in one code table;
- `/users/me` exposes permissions for frontend gating;
- 401 vs 403 split so forbidden actions don't log users out;
- a last-admin guard;
- PR1 (expand) then PR2 (drop `is_superuser`).

The human wants proof it works before production: scenario runs per role plus a migration rehearsal (upgrade/read-back/downgrade/upgrade). There's a ~1h timebox and no bonus for many tests or docs, so stay lean.

